I've implemented the parallel Smith-Waterman algorithm by processing matrix anti-diagonals in parallel, a standard approach for this problem. A ForkJoinPool manages a bounded thread pool, matching available processors to prevent oversubscription. The outer loop handles anti-diagonals sequentially to respect data dependencies, while the inner loop parallelizes cell computations within each anti-diagonal using IntStream.parallel(). A sequential fallback is included for small inputs to avoid parallelization overhead. Next, I'll build a test harness to validate correctness and determinism against the original sequential version.

