The performance test shows a significant slowdown, likely due to high synchronization overhead from joining after each small anti-diagonal calculation. While a cyclic barrier could be a better synchronization method, a simpler fix is to increase the SEQUENTIAL_THRESHOLD to ensure parallelism is only used for larger matrices where it can overcome the overhead. I'll adjust the threshold in SmithWatermanParallel.java and rerun the performance test.

